<h2>Integration recipes</h2>

<h3>Cursor</h3>
<pre><code>Settings → Models → Add custom model
Base URL: https://api.altkey.app/v1
Model name: claude-sonnet-4-5
API key: sk-alt-...</code></pre>

<h3>OpenAI Python SDK</h3>
<pre><code>from openai import OpenAI
client = OpenAI(base_url="https://api.altkey.app/v1", api_key="sk-alt-...")
r = client.chat.completions.create(model="claude-sonnet-4-5", messages=[{"role":"user","content":"hi"}])
print(r.choices[0].message.content)</code></pre>

<h3>curl</h3>
<pre><code>curl https://api.altkey.app/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-alt-..." \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"gemini-2.5-flash","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"hello"}],"stream":true}'</code></pre>

<h2 id="risk">The risk picture</h2>
<div class="card">
<p>This service operates against the ToS of Claude, ChatGPT, and Gemini. Specifically:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Anthropic <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/consumer-terms" target="_blank">prohibits</a> reverse-engineering and unauthorized programmatic access. In January 2026 they enforced against OpenClaw, OpenCode, Roo Code, and Goose.</li>
  <li>OpenAI prohibits automation/scripts against ChatGPT Plus. Detection patterns: account suspension is the typical outcome.</li>
  <li>Google prohibits automated access to Gemini Advanced.</li>
</ul>
<p>What we do to minimize your risk:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Forward your captured User-Agent + Accept-Language to keep the request fingerprint consistent with your normal browser.</li>
  <li>Limit concurrent in-flight requests per session.</li>
  <li>Route through Cloudflare edge PoPs near your likely region (based on captured timezone).</li>
  <li>Soft-cap at 1000 requests/day per provider so a runaway script doesn't trigger a hard suspension.</li>
</ul>
<p>What we cannot prevent:</p>
<ul>
  <li>A provider noticing the same session token used from a residential IP + Cloudflare IP within the same minute.</li>
  <li>A provider deciding to deploy a heuristic that targets this category and silently suspending all detected accounts.</li>
  <li>A provider legal team sending us a cease-and-desist that forces a shutdown.</li>
</ul>
<p>If we get a cease-and-desist or a subpoena, we will shut down within 24 hours and publish the reason. The OSS self-host build (<a href="https://github.com/SenGuru/altkey">github.com/SenGuru/altkey</a>) keeps working forever — point it at <code>http://127.0.0.1:8787</code> instead of <code>https://api.altkey.app</code>.</p>
</div>

